# Testing & Scripts

## Running Tests

```bash
yarn test                        # Complete proof (globally locked across worktrees)
yarn test:changed                # Affected tests since main + local changes
yarn test:workspace @aflow/schemas # One workspace through the root config
yarn test:file path/to/test.ts   # One or more explicit files
./scripts/test-flows.sh all      # All API integration tests
./scripts/test-flows.sh agent    # Agent flow only
./scripts/test-flows.sh chat-history  # Chat history only
./scripts/test-flows.sh basic    # Basic flows
```

Use the focused root commands for iteration. If a complete `yarn test` waits behind another
worktree, leave it queued or keep working with a focused command; never start a second broad Vitest
or workspace-level parallel run to bypass the lock.

## Seeding Flows

```bash
yarn db:seed                     # Seed sample flows to DB (via API)
npx tsx scripts/seed-flows.ts    # Same, direct execution
```

To add a new seed flow: edit `scripts/seed-flows.ts`, add to the `flows` array.
Format: `{ name, slug, version, steps[], startStepId?, stateVariables? }`.

## Test Flow Files (inline configs)

Test flows live in `scripts/test-flows/` as JSON files. These use the inline `flowConfig` API
(POST /v1/runs with `flowConfig` instead of `flowId`) — no database required.

To add a new test flow:
1. Create `scripts/test-flows/my-test.json`
2. Add a test function in `scripts/test-flows.sh`
3. Register in the `case "$TEST_FILTER"` switch

## Database Management

```bash
yarn infra:up                    # Start Postgres + Redis
yarn infra:reset                 # Wipe and reinitialize (runs init-db.sql)
yarn infra:tools                 # Start with pgAdmin (8080) + Redis Commander (8081)
```

Database is initialized by `scripts/init-db.sql` which runs on container creation.
Schema changes: edit `packages/database/src/schema/` and run `yarn db:push`.

## macOS Compatibility

- Use `sed '$d'` instead of `head -n -1` (macOS head doesn't support negative counts)
- Use `python3` not `python` for JSON parsing in shell scripts

## Adding New Operations to Tests

1. Implement the executor handler
2. Register in the operation registry (`packages/schemas`)
3. Build schemas: `yarn workspace @aflow/schemas build`
4. Add a test flow JSON in `scripts/test-flows/`
5. Add a test function in `scripts/test-flows.sh`
6. Add a seed flow in `scripts/seed-flows.ts` for UI testing
